# --------------------------------------------------------------- export-ignore
#
# What a PHP consumer downloads when Composer installs nebula-token/nebula-token.
#
# Packagist reads composer.json from a repository ROOT only, so the manifest for
# the PHP package is this repository's root composer.json — and this repository
# holds ten languages. Composer builds a package's dist archive with
# `git archive`, which honours export-ignore, so the rules below are what keep a
# PHP consumer from downloading a Rust crate, a Maven pom and a LaTeX paper into
# their vendor/ directory.
#
# Two things to know before editing:
#
#   * These rules affect the ARCHIVE ONLY. `git clone` and `actions/checkout`
#     ignore export-ignore entirely, so CI, the Docker harness and all ten
#     conformance suites still see the whole tree — including spec/, which every
#     runner locates by walking up from its own source file.
#   * Composer's `composer archive` reads only the ROOT .gitattributes, while
#     GitHub's zipball honours nested ones too. Keeping every rule here means the
#     two produce the same payload; a rule left in packages/php/.gitattributes
#     would be silently skipped by one of them.
#
# The payload is verified, not assumed:
#     composer archive --format=tar --dir=/tmp && tar -tf /tmp/nebula-token.tar
#
# What must SURVIVE: composer.json, LICENSE, README.md, SPECIFICATION.md, and
# packages/php minus its test suite — including
# packages/php/skills/nebula-token-php/, the agent skill in installable form.

# The nine other implementations.
/packages/typescript export-ignore
/packages/python     export-ignore
/packages/go         export-ignore
/packages/rust       export-ignore
/packages/java       export-ignore
/packages/csharp     export-ignore
/packages/dart       export-ignore
/packages/ruby       export-ignore
/packages/elixir     export-ignore

# Project machinery: normative to the repository, dead weight in vendor/.
# spec/ goes with it — the vectors are run from a checkout and never from an
# installed package (RELEASING.md step 6), and shipping 84 conformance cases to
# every consumer would imply otherwise. /skills is only the index README that
# points at the ten skills; the PHP skill itself lives inside the PHP package,
# at packages/php/skills/nebula-token-php/SKILL.md, and ships with it.
/docs    export-ignore
/spec    export-ignore
/scripts export-ignore
/docker  export-ignore
/assets  export-ignore
/skills  export-ignore

# Dot-files: CI, editor, link-checker and agent configuration. None of it means
# anything outside a clone of this repository.
#
# .claude-plugin/marketplace.json is the strongest case of the lot. It is the
# agent-skill catalogue for all ten languages, and nine of its ten `source`
# paths — ./packages/typescript, ./packages/python and the rest — are
# export-ignored above. Shipping it would put a catalogue in vendor/ whose
# entries point at directories the archive does not contain: worse than absent,
# because it reads as authoritative. The manifest is repository metadata, it is
# consumed from a clone by `npx skills add` and `/plugin marketplace add`, and
# nobody installs plugins out of a PHP dependency directory. packages/php's own
# skill is unaffected — it lives at packages/php/skills/nebula-token-php/ and
# still ships.
/.github        export-ignore
/.claude        export-ignore
/.claude-plugin export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
/.editorconfig  export-ignore
/.lycheeignore  export-ignore
/sonar-project.properties export-ignore

# Agent instructions for contributors to THIS repository. AGENTS.md tells an
# agent how a spec change lands across ten languages and what never to delete
# from this working tree; CLAUDE.md is a one-line bridge to it. Neither means
# anything inside a PHP consumer's vendor/, and AGENTS.md is 12 KB of rules
# about a repository they do not have. They are the last two root files that
# were shipping only because this deny-list had not named them.
/AGENTS.md      export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md      export-ignore

# The PHP test suite. Its runners walk up to spec/, which is export-ignored
# above, so shipping them would ship a suite that cannot run.
/packages/php/tests                 export-ignore
/packages/php/phpunit.xml           export-ignore
/packages/php/.phpunit.result.cache export-ignore

# Repository governance. LICENSE, README.md and SPECIFICATION.md are NOT here:
# Packagist renders the README, every published artefact carries the grant
# (scripts/check-licenses.mjs), and packages/php/README.md links to
# ../../SPECIFICATION.md — a link that has to keep resolving inside vendor/.
/CHANGELOG.md       export-ignore
/CITATION.cff       export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
/COMPATIBILITY.md   export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md    export-ignore
/GOVERNANCE.md      export-ignore
/RELEASING.md       export-ignore
/SECURITY.md        export-ignore
/SUPPORT.md         export-ignore
/VERSIONING.md      export-ignore
